# Borough alerts. Installed at /etc/cron.d/rentmap-alerts (scp this file;
# never hand-edit on the box — see deploy/cron-rentmap-growth).
#
# Every 10 minutes: refresh Housing Connect, welcome new sign-ups, mail what
# is new. "The minute a lottery opens" is a promise about THIS cadence — the
# Housing Connect refresh is one cheap POST and the run is a no-op when
# nothing changed, so ten minutes costs nothing.
#
# One email a day per address, across every job (growth/mailcap.py): the first
# new item of the day goes out at once, later ones are held per subscriber
# and lead the next day's first email.
#
# Replaces the twice-daily /etc/cron.d/rentmap-housingconnect: the wrapper
# writes the same housing_connect.json, so that file is removed on install.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
*/10 * * * * root /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1

# Below here the clock is New York's. Both lines sit AFTER the 06:20 ET
# saved-building run (deploy/cron-rentmap-saved): someone who is both an
# account holder and a borough subscriber gets the personal email and, having
# had today's one, is skipped here — the round-up content overlaps anyway.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York

# 06:35 daily: first-week round-up for sign-ups that have had only the welcome.
35 6 * * * root /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh --nudge >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1

# 06:40 Tuesdays: the weekly round-up — opened this week, closing this week.
40 6 * * 2 root /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh --weekly >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1
